# Implementation Plan: Resume-Quality Features for EchoReads

This implementation plan details the addition of four high-impact, resume-quality features to the EchoReads project:
1. **AI Integration (Gemini & RAG)**: Live chatbot utilizing Gemini AI API and content retrieval from the MongoDB book catalog.
2. **Interactive UX (E-Book Reader & Text-to-Speech)**: Custom in-browser e-book reader page with styling customization, bookmarks, and a synchronized TTS audiobook highlighter.
3. **Payment & Commerce (Stripe & Digital Access Control)**: Sandbox Stripe checkout flow with backend digital access control restricting content reading to purchased books only.
4. **Backend Performance (Redis Caching & Fuzzy Search)**: Fault-tolerant Redis caching layer and MongoDB text-based search.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **API Credentials Needed in `.env`**:
> To run these features fully, you will need to add the following variables to your `backend/.env` file:
> * `GEMINI_API_KEY`: A free API key from Google AI Studio.
> * `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` & `STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`: Free sandbox keys from a Stripe Developer Account.
> * `REDIS_URL`: URL of your Redis instance (defaults to `redis://localhost:6379`).
>
> **Graceful Fallbacks Built-in**:
> If these credentials or instances are not available locally:
> * Gemini will fall back to a mock responsive AI matching system.
> * Stripe will fall back to a mock instant successful payment process.
> * Redis will gracefully fall back to querying MongoDB directly without crashing the server.

