### Track 3: Payment & Commerce (Stripe Checkout & Access Control)

#### [MODIFY] [backend/routes/purchases.js](file:///c:/Users/sande/Academics/web%20page/EchoReads/backend/routes/purchases.js)
* **Goal**: Implement Stripe SDK backend payment endpoints.
* **Endpoints**:
  * `POST /api/purchases/create-checkout-session`: Formulates Stripe session containing cart line items and prices.
  * `GET /api/purchases/stripe-success`: Verification handler endpoint that confirms a paid Stripe session, records purchases in MongoDB, and clears the cart.
* **Mock Fallback**: If Stripe secret keys are not configured, allow checkouts to complete instantly as a mock cash-on-delivery/mock payment.

#### [MODIFY] [backend/routes/books.js](file:///c:/Users/sande/Academics/web%20page/EchoReads/backend/routes/books.js)
* **Goal**: Add a secure `/api/books/:id/read` endpoint.
* **Security check**: Verify if the logged-in user has purchased the book (`Purchase.findOne({ user: userId, book: bookId })`). If not, deny access to the book's full `content` (returning a 403 error).

#### [MODIFY] [frontend/checkout.html](file:///c:/Users/sande/Academics/web%20page/EchoReads/frontend/checkout.html)
* **Goal**: Embed Stripe.js. Render a "Pay Securely with Stripe" button.

