### Track 4: Backend Performance (Redis Caching & Fuzzy Search)

#### [NEW] [backend/utils/cache.js](file:///c:/Users/sande/Academics/web%20page/EchoReads/backend/utils/cache.js)
* **Goal**: Implement a wrapper around `ioredis` to manage caching.
* **Fault Tolerance**: Catch connection errors. If Redis is down, log a warning and fallback to normal MongoDB queries.

#### [MODIFY] [backend/routes/books.js](file:///c:/Users/sande/Academics/web%20page/EchoReads/backend/routes/books.js)
* **Goal**: Cache catalog queries (`GET /api/books` and `GET /api/books/genres`) in Redis with a 5-minute TTL. Clear the cache whenever a book is created, updated, or deleted.
* **Fuzzy Text Search**: Implement MongoDB text index on the `Book` schema (`title`, `author`, `genre`). Modify searching behavior to use text indexes for typo-tolerant matching.

